<td><!-- #BeginEditable "cardstrategy" -->
<p>
<b>Son Of Skywalker</b><br>

By Boone Adkins<br><br> Son Of Skywalker is a great card.  For game players: He is a little bit restricted and costly in deployment, but it’s worth what you get.  The power of five is high and an ability of five is good and it allows a battle destiny.  Also, that ability allows a good chance for a successful destiny draw for Sense and Alter.  And last, that ability of five helps with Jedi tests.  Now don't be sad about having to deploy only on Dagobah or Cloud City.   <br><br>That restriction can be of some use.  You can deploy him on Dagobah, regardless of the location deployment restrictions, a useful thing for Jedi training.  Like the typical pilot, Son Of Skywalker adds two to the power of any starship he pilots.  He is immune to attrition less than four.  And last, you can deploy a lightsaber to the same location as Son Of Skywalker.
<br><br>
Combos:
<br><br>
Son Of Skywalker + Any card that allows you to peek at the top of your Reserve Deck - 
a guaranteed good battle destiny.
<br><br>
Son Of Skywalker + Courage Of A Skywalker (In hand) + This Is More Like It (In hand) + Smoke Screen (In hand) -
Lots of laughs for you, your opponent looses tons of force!
<br><br>
Son Of Skywalker + Chewbacca + Wookiee Strangle + Jedi tests + Apprentice + Lots of At Peace cards -
Now Vader gets choked for a change!
<br><br>
Son Of Sky walker + Teamwork cards and their partners -
A heck of a lot of attrition and battle damage
<br><br>
Escorted Son Of Skywalker + Captive Fury (Lost function) -
Bye Bye Bounty Hunter!




</p>
